------------------------------------------------------------------------
Is it possible for Str_copy or Str_concat to call assert to verify
that the destination memory area specified by the caller is large
enough? Explain.

It is not possible for Str_copy and Str_concat to call assert
to ensure that the destination memory is large enough. When you pass
the destination string to either function, it becomes a pointer to 
the first character of the destination string. Therefore, there is no
implicit information that can be extracted from the pointer to know
how much memory the compiler set aside on the stack for that string. 
Calling sizeof within the function would return 8 on 64-bit systems, 
as that is the size of the pointer.

